# Review routing for CI-critical paths. Requires an approval from one of the
# listed owners when a PR touches a matching path (enforced via branch
# protection's "require review from Code Owners" on main).
#
# Notes on how GitHub evaluates this file:
#   - gitignore-style patterns; the LAST matching pattern wins.
#   - Owners must have write access or the rule silently does not bind.
#   - Any single listed owner's approval satisfies the rule; an author's own
#     approval never counts, so keep at least two owners per rule.
#   - Only the copy of this file on the PR's base branch is enforced, so a PR
#     that rewrites these rules is still judged by the old ones.
#
# No default (catch-all) owner: paths not listed here keep the normal review
# flow.
#
# Two groups of paths are protected, for two different reasons. A path belongs
# here when a change to it changes what CI executes, or with what rights, so
# that the review is routed to someone who will look at it in those terms.

# ── Workflows ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every workflow file, whichever runner it targets.

/.github/                                        @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130

# ── Self-hosted runner ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Code and configuration that decide what executes on the shared self-hosted
# "nashua" box. The same paths are listed in the `gate` job of
# .github/workflows/playwright.yml and ohif-downstream.yml; keep the two in
# step. They do different jobs: the gate keeps a fork PR off the box until its
# change is merged, and these rules put a code owner in front of the merge.
#
# The last three do not exist in the repository today. That is deliberate: pnpm
# executes a root pnpmfile if one appears, and reads .npmrc for the registry and
# install policy, so the rules have to be here before the files are.

/scripts/ci/                                     @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/scripts/run-playright.sh                        @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/scripts/link-ohif-cornerstone-node-modules.mjs  @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/preinstall.js                                   @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/package.json                                    @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/pnpm-lock.yaml                                  @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                             @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/.npmrc                                          @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/.pnpmfile.cjs                                   @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/pnpmfile.cjs                                    @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130

# ── Release pipeline ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scripts that .github/workflows/publish.yml runs on every merge to main, with
# `contents: write` and `id-token: write` — i.e. with the rights to push the
# version commit and tag, create the release, and publish to npm. A fork PR
# cannot trigger that workflow, but a change merged from one is executed by it,
# so the review before merge is the only check. These do NOT belong in the
# `gate` lists above: they never run on the self-hosted box.

/scripts/release-mode.mjs                        @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
/scripts/workspace-packages.mjs                  @jbocce @sedghi @wayfarer3130
